# ============================================================================
# DUEL environment — copy to .env.local and fill in.
# NEVER commit real keys. The browser bundle only ever sees NEXT_PUBLIC_* vars.
# ============================================================================

# ---- Supabase (safe for the browser) --------------------------------------
# Dashboard → Project Settings → API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...anon-key...

# ---- Cloudflare R2 (SERVER-ONLY — never exposed to the frontend) ----------
# Dashboard → R2 → Manage API Tokens
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=your-account-id
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-access-key
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-secret
R2_BUCKET_NAME=duel-media
# Optional: public custom domain / CDN base if you later serve some objects publicly
# R2_PUBLIC_URL=https://cdn.yourdomain.com

# Optional (testing / S3-compatible gateways only). Leave UNSET in production —
# lib/r2/client.ts derives the real R2 endpoint from R2_ACCOUNT_ID.
# R2_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9000
# R2_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true

# ============================================================================
# ⚠️  REQUIRED: do NOT let the AWS SDK add default integrity checksums
#
# @aws-sdk/client-s3 >= 3.729 turns on "default integrity protections"
# (requestChecksumCalculation / responseChecksumValidation = WHEN_SUPPORTED).
# That silently folds extra parameters into EVERY presigned URL:
#
#   PutObject → x-amz-checksum-crc32=AAAAAA%3D%3D  (CRC32 of an EMPTY body)
#               x-amz-sdk-checksum-algorithm=CRC32
#   GetObject → x-amz-checksum-mode=ENABLED
#
# Cloudflare R2 does not implement `x-amz-checksum-mode`, so a signed GET that
# carries it is answered with an error instead of the object. The media URL then
# never streams, <video> fires onError, and the player shows "Video unavailable"
# even though the upload itself reported success.
#
# lib/r2/client.ts already pins both options to WHEN_REQUIRED, which keeps
# presigned URLs to exactly the parameters Cloudflare documents. If you ever
# construct an S3Client for R2 elsewhere, you MUST set them there too.
# Verify with: npm run test:media
# ============================================================================

# ============================================================================
# R2 BUCKET CORS (required for direct browser uploads via presigned PUT)
# Set once in Cloudflare dashboard → R2 → your bucket → Settings → CORS policy,
# or via the Cloudflare API. Replace https://yourdomain.com with your origin
# (and http://localhost:3000 while developing):
#
# [
#   {
#     "AllowedOrigins": ["http://localhost:3000", "https://yourdomain.com"],
#     "AllowedMethods": ["GET", "PUT"],
#     "AllowedHeaders": ["content-type"],
#     "ExposeHeaders": ["etag"],
#     "MaxAgeSeconds": 3600
#   }
# ]
# ============================================================================

# ============================================================================
# SUPABASE SETUP ORDER
#   1. Fill in the two NEXT_PUBLIC_* values above (auth starts working).
#   2. Run supabase/duel/INSPECT_BEFORE_MIGRATION.sql (read-only report),
#      then supabase/migrations/20260920000000_duel_platform.sql in the SQL Editor
#      (challenges, streaks, recommendations, RLS, seed data).
#   3. Fill in the four R2_* values + bucket CORS (permanent media uploads).
# The app gracefully runs in demo mode until each step is done.
# ============================================================================
